{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אם אין", :translit "im ayin", :gloss "if not / or not"} {:he "ד'", :translit "dalet", :gloss "four (abbreviation)"} {:he "אם אין אתה", :translit "im ayin atah", :gloss "if you are not"} {:he "אם אין אתה שומע לי", :translit "im ayin atah shome'a li", :gloss "if you do not listen to me"} {:he "היש בה עץ אם אין", :translit "ha'yesh bah etz im ayin", :gloss "is there a tree in it or not"} {:he "היש ה' בקרבנו אם אין", :translit "ha'yesh Hashem b'kirbenu im ayin", :gloss "is Hashem among us or not"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["אם אין"]} {:kind :other, :note "Four occurrences of אם אין linked thematically: three concern war that results from not heeding counsel, the fourth is our verse."}], :frame {:text "Ahithophel counseled Absalom to pursue David immediately while David was weak, saying \"אם אין אתה שומע לי\" — Hushai countered the counsel and Absalom did not heed Ahithophel, leading to Absalom's defeat in battle (II Samuel 17:6-14). The spies were sent to scout the land and reported \"היש בה עץ אם אין\" (Numbers 13:20); the Sages state that because Israel sent spies they needed weapons for war (Tanchuma, Sh'lach 4). In our verse Israel asks \"היש ה' בקרבנו אם אין\" and immediately Amalek attacks (Exodus 17:7-8). The Ba'al HaTurim links all four instances of אם אין to the theme that questioning or not heeding leads to war.", :sources ["II Samuel 17:6-14" "Numbers 13:20" "Exodus 17:7-8" "Tanchuma Sh'lach 4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["אם אין"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "אם אין", :refs ["Exodus 17:7" "Exodus 22:2" "Exodus 33:15" "Numbers 13:20" "2 Samuel 17:6" "Proverbs 22:27" "Job 33:33"], :n 7, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Four occurrences of אם אין linked thematically: three concern war that results from not heeding counsel, the fourth is our verse.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:16:52.693894386Z", :model "glm-5.2"}